delete from sermons where service_date = '2026-08-23' and title = 'Living Under The Rule Of The KING';
insert into sermons (service_date, title, preacher, is_guest, occasion, series, anchor_scripture, thesis, summary, youtube_url, notes)
values (
  '2026-08-23',
  'Living Under The Rule Of The KING',
  'Rev Ifeayinchukwu Obi',
  true,
  null,
  null,
  'John 3:3-7',
  E'The pearl of great price is not a distant reward but the King already living inside the believer - so the honest question is not whether we have found it, but why our response to holding it is timid, lukewarm and civilised when the men in the parable responded with joy.',
  E'Third Sunday of Rev Obi''s kingdom thread and the one where the parables stop being illustrations and become a mirror. He spends the first ten minutes revising 9 August: kingdom is king plus domain, a realm where the King is ruling, and the two Matthew 13 parables of the treasure in the field and the pearl of great price. Both men found something, sold everything they had, and the word for their response was joy.\n\nThen he asks why Jesus taught in parables at all, and gives an answer that carries the whole message. A parable is a provocation. To those with ears that do not hear it closes; to anyone in whom it wakes a desire to know more, He comes running. When you set out to explore these things, the Lord meets you immediately, and that is the point of teaching this way.\n\nHe then names the pearl without hedging. It is not a distant reward and not an abstraction: it is already inside you, the Holy Spirit, the King eternal and immortal, the only true God. You have found it whether you believe it or not. Which sets up the turn the sermon actually rests on. The two men responded with joy; our response does not match. At best it is timid, at best lukewarm, at best civilised. Not from doubt, but because we do not know the value of what is inside us. Alongside it he sets the value of a soul: what will it profit a man to gain the whole world and lose his soul, meaning one soul is worth more to Christ than the whole world, and any circumstance held next to that shrinks.\n\nFrom there, entry and evidence. The kingdom is entered by a new birth, exactly as Jesus told Nicodemus in the morning''s reading: born of water is the physical birth, born again is the second one into the spirit realm, and Nicodemus got lost because he assumed a second birth into the same realm. The evidence of new birth is obedience, and obedience is the mechanism of the King''s rule, put in a line hard to argue with: if you hear his word and you do not obey it, he is not ruling, you are ruling. The Spirit already inside knows every decision facing you and is waiting only on your response, and his own testimony is that guidance arrived unprompted, not after fasting.\n\nRepentance he treats as direction rather than mood. John the Baptist''s change your mind means change your perspective on life; you cannot keep walking the way you are walking and expect to be inside the kingdom. And the kingdom is not a distant dream to be entered at death, it is here now, which is precisely why the change of mind is urgent.\n\nHis own story carries the cost. Chasing an executive directorship at a bank, his heart moving toward money because money was ruling, and being shown both that this was not the plan and what waited at the end of that road. He stopped, was called into missions about two weeks later, and has not drawn a salary from anyone since 1998 - offered not as a boast but as evidence that the King does not send you to war at your own cost. If He wants you somewhere, the fare is there; the trouble starts when you decide to do or die to arrange it yourself.\n\nThe transcript ends mid-sentence at 29:59 as he opens a new section on what the apostles preached. The final eleven minutes, including any conclusion or altar call, are not on record.',
  null,
  E'SOURCE: TurboScribe transcript supplied by Bolaji on 23 August 2026, from the service recording. FIRST 30 MINUTES ONLY - the free tier stops at 30:00 and the sermon runs about 41 minutes. full_text ends mid-sentence at 29:59 on ''What did his disciples preach? What did the apostles like Paul, what did they preach?''\n\n>> THE LAST ~11 MINUTES ARE NOT ON RECORD. Any conclusion, application or altar call is unseen. Do NOT write a closing sequence, caption or carousel that claims to land where the sermon landed. If the full audio is transcribed later, update full_text and clear this flag.\n\nATTRIBUTION TO CHECK: he says ''the bible says, the king does not send you to war at your own cost'' and adds ''That''s Jesus.'' The nearest scripture is Paul, 1 Corinthians 9:7 - who goeth a warfare any time at his own charges. Not a saying of Jesus in the gospels. Do not caption it as a quotation of Jesus. The point itself stands and is his own.\n\nUNVERIFIED FIGURE: he reports that searching the KJV for the exact phrase ''enter into the kingdom'' returns 13 references, 12 of them from Jesus. Given as recap from two weeks earlier. Verify independently before putting the number on a slide.\n\nTRANSCRIPT GARBLES corrected in full_text: pear to pearl throughout; ''according to Brodoby'' to ''according to my reading''; ''no skating, no bowling'' to ''no scathing, no burning''; ''the kingdom is communal'' to ''the kingdom is that way''. Nigerian English and his spoken rhythm retained deliberately.\n\nSERIES CONTINUITY: this is the third Sunday of the kingdom thread (9 Aug ''Enter Into The Kingdom'' was the previous one he refers to as ''last week'' and also as ''two weeks ago'' - he corrects himself aloud and is inconsistent thereafter). 9 Aug covered the treasure in the field, Matthew 13:44; 23 Aug covers the pearl, Matthew 13:45-46. He explicitly links them. Not formally badged as a named series.\n\nIS_GUEST: true. Rev Obi is a guest minister and the badge appears on the 23 Aug thumbnail and run sheet.\n\nNAME SPELLING: ''Ifeayinchukwu'' as used across every published asset. It has also appeared as ''Ifeanyichukwu'' (21 June 2026). UNRESOLVED - confirm with him before further publishing.'
);

-- ============================================================
-- PART 2 of 4 - the sermon body (one long E'' string, own statement)
-- ============================================================
update sermons
   set full_text = E'NEAR-VERBATIM TRANSCRIPT, FIRST 30 MINUTES ONLY of a 41-minute sermon. The TurboScribe free tier stops at 30:00 and the record ends mid-sentence. Auto-transcript garbles corrected; see the notes column before quoting.\n\nIt''s not just that I fancy the subject matter, so I come and say it before you know. It''s because he has pointed it to me for a very long time, very long time ago. And it helped me to stand where I am standing today.\n\nAnd he has always undertaken for me. I''ve shared a few testimonies with you here. It''s not because I can pray.\n\nIt''s not because I am worth anything. But it''s because Christ died for me, and I''m a bona fide citizen of the kingdom of God. When we talk about the kingdom of God, as we said last week, what does the kingdom of God mean? And what does it mean to you? We said last week that the word kingdom is a combination of two words.\n\nKing and domain. King and domain. A domain, a realm, or an area where the king is ruling.\n\nThat''s simply the kingdom. So don''t look at it very far away. Last week we looked at Matthew chapter 13 verse 44.\n\nWhere the Lord Jesus Christ was describing, he gave us a parable about kingdom. I don''t know, we didn''t discuss it, but I want to remind you that Jesus taught in parables. You need to ask yourself, why did our Lord teach in parables? I''m sure you know.\n\nOne of the reasons why he taught in parables is so that it will provoke a desire inside you to know. To know more. If it does not provoke a desire for you to know more, that word is finished there.\n\nHe said to the disciples who were asking him, why is it that you''re always teaching parables? I have such a time in myself. He said, it''s given to you to know, but it''s not given to them. So when he''s speaking to people to whom it''s not given, to people who have ears but they don''t hear, people who have eyes but they don''t see, if it does not wake up a desire for them to know, that''s the end of the matter.\n\nBut if it wakes up a desire, he runs to meet you immediately. See all these things we are talking about in church. When you set out to explore them, the Lord will meet with you immediately.\n\nAnd that''s why he teaches in parables. So he gave us a parable of the man who went to look for a goodly treasure. He called it treasure of inestimable value.\n\nAnd we tried to tell ourselves, what is a treasure of inestimable value? Inestimable, you cannot estimate the value of that treasure. But the only thing we added to it was to explain that treasure by the Lord''s word about our soul. Where he said, what will it profit a man to gain the whole world and then lose his soul? The Lord was saying it that that man is foolish, who will gain the whole world and at the end he will lose his soul.\n\nThe Lord was telling us that one soul, your soul, is greater than the value of the whole world to him. Whenever we say this, people don''t understand. Think about it.\n\nMeditate on it because it has to do with you and me. The value of your soul to God. Then bring around you the circumstances that you are facing and you forget that you are valued more than the whole world to Christ.\n\nIf you are able to remember that, in any circumstance, that circumstance will die. That travail will finish. You will walk through it with no scathing, no burning, nothing will happen to you.\n\nAll because you know the value of your soul to the Lord Jesus Christ. So this man found the treasure of inestimable value where in a field. This is a field.\n\nManchester is a field. So many, but let''s not go there. He found it.\n\nHe was so joyful at finding it. What did he do? He buried it back, covered it with sand, and did what? Ran back to his business, ran back to his house, sold everything that he had so that he would do what? Buy, not the treasure. He bought the field surrounding that so he would not contest with anybody, any kingdom, any desire, any attractions.\n\nNo, he bought the entire field because of that treasure. In verse 45 again, he gave us another example of the one that was looking after a goodly pearl. You know, who found it and did what? Also went back and sold everything.\n\nAnd the question we had last week for you was, look at the responses of these people who found this thing. Their response was full of joy. And we said to ourselves, we have found the same pearl.\n\nWe have found the pearl of inestimable value. You and I, you have found it. You better pronounce that to yourself.\n\nYou have found it. Because that pearl is where? Is inside of you right now. The precious Holy Spirit, the King that is eternal, the King that is immortal, the only true God is inside.\n\nWhether you believe it or not. You have found it. But what response are you giving to finding it? And the response sometimes is not correct.\n\nLook at the joyful response of those two in Matthew 13, 44 and 45. You yourself, what was your response? Or what is your response? That was the question we left last week. We took ourselves to Matthew 6, verse 33 where the Lord was helping us, guiding us, bringing us into the right line.\n\nSays we should do what? Seek first the kingdom of God. And all these things which do not compare, they will be added to you. No matter, even if he says it a hundred times, he is not going to make you.\n\nYou are the one that will prioritise those things. He is not going to come and prioritise your life for you. You are the one that will take the decision to say, ah, this is not important.\n\nThis is more important for me. Only you can make that decision. But the Lord has guided us into it and that is what he wants to drive our life.\n\nFinding the kingdom first. He says because all these things will be added onto us. Then we talked about that the kingdom was the pathway to abundant life.\n\nJohn chapter 10, verse 10. The Lord Jesus Christ said, I have come to give you what? Life. And to give it to you more abundantly.\n\nHe is the king. Christ is the king. You know, Christ is the king.\n\nAnd if he has come and done something for you, something that takes care of you, that''s why we call him a true king, not like the kings of the earth. A true king takes care of all his subjects, all his citizens. Takes care.\n\nWhat they wear. What they eat. Where they live.\n\nHe takes care. That''s why he says, look at the birds of the air. What about you? What about you? If he takes care of the birds of the air, the fishes of the sea, why do you think he wouldn''t take care of you? The only person he made in his own image.\n\nWell, we are provoking thoughts here by revising. Okay. And we asked last week.\n\nWe checked Google last week. You know, you remember. Two weeks ago.\n\nSorry. Forgive me. You know.\n\nTwo weeks ago. We checked Google. What is abundant life? And when we read what he said abundant life was, we said, if you found such a thing, what would you do? Everybody professed that joy will fill their heart to receive it.\n\nIsn''t that what we said last week? Okay. So, the Christian dilemma as we ended up last week was that we appear to have found the kingdom, but our response does not support it. At best, our response is timid.\n\nTimid. Because we don''t know the value of what is inside us. You know.\n\nAt best, it is timid. At best, it is lukewarm. At best, it is civilised.\n\nLeave those people in Africa that clap hands and all those things. You know. Some people regard it as it''s not a big deal.\n\nThis question of a kingdom is not a big deal. Some people will even tell you don''t get carried away by it. That''s our response.\n\nOkay. And this is what the Bible is talking about. Because that man for joy at the revelation, the man heeded back and went to sell everything.\n\nThat''s just a reminder of two weeks ago. There is more to it, but I cannot spend my whole time revising what we did last two weeks. Okay.\n\nBut today, I want to bring something else to us. Let us pray. Precious Heavenly Father, you are our stronghold.\n\nYes, your word says that when troubles come, you are our hiding place. But that same word says that you will never, we know you, faithful God, that you will never forsake those who put their trust in you. Father, we put our trust in you.\n\nYou said if we acknowledge you and put our trust in you, you will direct our paths. Precious Father, as we listen to your word today, we ask for a direction to our paths. That we may live and bring praise and glory to your holy name.\n\nWe have prayed in Jesus'' name. Amen. Amen.\n\nThere is more to it, but I have to stop there because we can''t take it all. But that was last week. I brought my notes from last two weeks.\n\nToday, I would like us to go a little bit more. That was introductory. That was introductory two weeks ago.\n\nTo the kingdom of God. And it''s everything. It''s everything you should be focused on.\n\nAs a Christian. If you haven''t been focussing, begin. Begin.\n\nLet it occupy at least 80% of your Bible study time. You know, I challenged you two weeks ago. And I said, if you Googled, does anybody remember that? If you Googled King James Version of the Bible.\n\nThe old King James Version. And you put the word, in inverted commas, enter into the kingdom. If you search the King James Bible with that, it will give you 13 references.\n\nAnd 12 of that 13 references emanate from the Lord Jesus Christ. And why did I choose that? I chose that because it''s what he revealed to me. And I have studied it.\n\nI don''t know, from maybe 1984, 1985. It stipulates various conditions that will enable you to enter and inherit the kingdom. And we said two weeks ago that, according to the scripture we also read this morning.\n\nYou are born into this world, are you not, by your mother. There was water breaking before you came out of the womb. This world is a place, isn''t it? This physical world is a realm.\n\nAnd that''s the one you are born into. We said this two weeks ago. And we said for the kingdom of God, the Lord Jesus Christ instructed Nicodemus and all of us.\n\nBecause the kingdom of God is a place, isn''t it? It''s a realm. It''s not a physical place. Like this world is a physical place.\n\nBut the kingdom of God, like we talked about, king domain. A domain where the king is ruling. So the kingdom of God, like the Lord Jesus Christ says, does not come with observation.\n\nIf anybody tells you the kingdom of God is here or there, don''t listen to them. Jesus said because the kingdom of God is where? In you. The kingdom of God is in you.\n\nWhat does that mean? The king is in your heart. Waiting to rule over your life. He has died for you.\n\nHe''s given his life for you. Now you that are alive, you''ve been exchanged on the cross. The life you should live should be the life of Christ.\n\nIf you''re not living the life of Christ, you are wasting the blood of Jesus Christ. It''s true. It''s true.\n\nIt''s not a reproach. I just want you to think about it. If you are not living for Christ, Galatians 2 verse 20 tells us that we have been crucified with Christ.\n\nYes. Anybody who is saved, anybody who is born again, has chosen what happened on the cross. Believed what happened on the cross, is standing on it.\n\nThat''s why our sins are cleansed. Not only sins of yesterday, but sins of today and sins of tomorrow. It''s been cleansed.\n\nThey will no longer hold you. So that you will abandon yourself and surrender to God. So that God who is already inside you can live through you.\n\nI hope you''re getting me. I''m not going to preach. I''m just going to try my best to teach because this is something that should be taught.\n\nSo, we said the kingdom of God is entered by a new birth. Okay. Nicodemus said to the Lord Jesus Christ in John chapter 3, which we read this morning, verse 3 and verse 5. He said, except you are born again, you will not see the kingdom of God.\n\nIn verse 5, he says, except you are born of water, physical birth, according to my reading. Many theologians have their own interpretation, but that''s my own interpretation. And I know that by the spirit that I''m right.\n\nExcept you are born physically, you cannot be born again. Okay. Did you get me? You''re first born physically as you are.\n\nBy your mother, you are brought into this world. You are brought into this physical realm. And Jesus was telling Nicodemus, except you are born again.\n\nMany people get lost in thinking about that concept. Nicodemus got lost too. Remember what he said? Lord Jesus Christ, what do you mean? Do you mean as you enter back into my mother''s womb and be born? No, he''s not talking about being born into the same realm.\n\nYou''ve been born into this realm. The realm of the earth. That''s not what he''s talking about.\n\nHe''s talking about the spirit realm. So also, into the kingdom of God, you have to be born into it. Oh yes, that''s why you must be born again.\n\nHallelujah. Yes, we must be born again. Now, you ask yourself, what is the evidence that somebody is born again? In other words, if you''re born again, you believe what Christ did for you on the cross.\n\nThat he carried your sins. Therefore, you no longer live for yourself, but you live for him. So the evidence of being born again, for instance, is obedience.\n\nObedience to the word of God. Obedience to the word of your king. It''s the king that is inside you that wants to rule.\n\nFor him to rule, you have to hear his word. And you have to do what? Obey it. If you hear his word and you don''t obey it, he''s not ruling.\n\nYou are ruling. Hello? So it''s formed through surrender. You know that favourite song we sing at altar calls? I surrender all.\n\nI surrender all. My blessed saviour, I surrender. That''s actually what is happening at your new birth.\n\nWhen you become born again, that is the de facto effect it should have on you. You surrender. Acknowledge that the king lives inside you and the king is able to talk to you.\n\nHe''s able to guide you. He''s able to teach you. Remember? John chapter 14, verse 26.\n\nThe Lord Jesus Christ said, it''s better for you that I go away. So that the father will send his promise. When I go away, I will send another comforter.\n\nWho is the Holy Spirit. When he comes, verse 26 says, he will teach you all things. And will bring to bear upon your remembrance everything he has said.\n\nSo it''s not a hard job. If you allow the king who is inside, the spirit of the king is inside. The Holy Spirit is not physical.\n\nYeah? The Holy Spirit is a spirit. You are his body. You are the body that he uses.\n\nAnd he''s already inside. So every decision that is facing you, he already knows it. What he''s waiting for is what will be your response.\n\nEvery decision. Please, I''m not excluding anything. Every decision that faces you in life.\n\nHe wants to guide you. I share my testimony here. 27th of July, 1987 was the date I knew that the Holy Spirit was inside me.\n\nThe date I knew that he talked. He talked. I shared my testimony of the conception of my wife here.\n\nDidn''t I? I didn''t know he talked. I didn''t know he was inside. I didn''t know that he wanted to guide my life.\n\nI don''t like sharing this testimony about prayer because sometimes people think it''s not necessary to pray. Oh, I pray. I pray.\n\nBut most of the times when he intervenes, I can''t look back and say I was praying and fasting before he said something to me. Because something was going to threaten his destiny for me. He came to give me information.\n\nImmediately. What remains is whether you take that information or whether you stick by it and continue to walk. He wants to guide you.\n\nHe wants to lead you. This is not preaching, my brothers and my sisters. It''s something you must actualise for yourself.\n\nBecause that is the whole essence of being a Christian. If he doesn''t guide you or direct you, you''re what? Not only lost. Because that''s the way the children of this world or the simple English says you are a bastard.\n\nYou don''t have a father. But if you have a father, you must listen to your father and take guidance. So, we said two weeks ago.\n\nI''m sorry. I''m just refreshing you so that it will impact you. We said two weeks ago that Jesus did not preach any other thing.\n\nHe didn''t preach religion. He preached the kingdom. We refer to John the Baptist, right? When John the Baptist came, what did he preach? The kingdom of God is near.\n\nNear. All of you, change your mind. And we say changing your mind is change your perspective to life.\n\nIf you don''t change your perspective to life, you cannot see that kingdom. Neither can you enter it. In other words, you''re going this way.\n\nAnd John the Baptist is telling you the kingdom is that way. You must stop going this way. You must repent.\n\nAnd go towards where you know that the kingdom is. That''s what it means to change your mind. I mean to repent.\n\nYou change your mind about the way you''re going. You must change your mind. You cannot continue going the way you''re going and expect to be inside the kingdom.\n\nNo. It calls for repentance. Now, we said that Jesus did not preach religion.\n\nOr a distant dream. You know some of us think the kingdom of God is when we die. How Jesus will welcome us into the kingdom.\n\nNo, it''s not a distant dream. It''s something that is happening now. That''s why you must change your mind.\n\nThat''s why you must change your perspective. When you do, oh, you see the fruit that will come from it. I used to say to people, I would have died long ago.\n\nI would have died a despicable death. It''s not that death is anything. But I would have been lost.\n\nBut the Lord was gracious to me to show me. There''s a decision that will come in front of you. In fact, not a decision that will come.\n\nThere is where your heart is. Your heart is going this way. But the Lord instructed me that that is not his way.\n\nI was chasing to become an executive director of a bank. And he stopped me. You are after money.\n\nOf course, I''ve earned money. I''ve worked for international organisations. Worked for conglomerate commercial concerns.\n\nConsulted for... So my heart was moving in the direction of money. Because it was money that was ruling. He says, no, that''s not my plan for you.\n\nBut if you want to continue going that way, this is what is waiting for you. He showed me. It''s not that one is afraid of death.\n\nBut it''s what kind of death. I surrendered to him. I said, father, I''m sorry.\n\nI can''t tell you more. There''s a lot I could say to explain what I''m saying. But I just said, father, no, I will not go that way anymore.\n\nI stopped chasing that job. Then the following day, I was called into the work of missions. Not the following day.\n\nAbout two weeks later. And since then, I''ve been in mission. Because that''s his plan for my life.\n\nEven the work I did in international organisation. Banking and all those. He also arranged it himself.\n\nHe was God that directed me there. If I don''t have time. But when you get into bank and get to all those money places, your heart begins to buy into money.\n\nBut it''s not everybody that has that route. You must find your route and stick to it. And God was telling me, that''s not my route for you.\n\nIt may be for other people. But not for you. I can tell you that since that time in 1998, nobody has paid me a salary.\n\nNobody. Nobody can boast they paid me a salary. Till today.\n\nWhy am I telling you this? We talk about glorious riches in Christ Jesus. We are talking about we living in Christ Jesus. Christ in you, the hope of glory.\n\nEverything I do, I obey the king. If the king has not provided what I need to do that thing. The bible says, the king does not send you to war at your own cost.\n\nThat''s Jesus. He doesn''t send you to war at your own cost. If you are going to war and it''s at your own cost, that is not Jesus.\n\nYou need to check yourself. That''s your own war that you are going to. But whenever he sends you to war, he''s already paid the price.\n\nHe''s paid the cost. If I''m supposed to come to UK, the money will be there. I don''t earn a salary to buy a ticket.\n\nBut the money for that ticket will be there. Somehow. It''s only when you look for it in a particular way, that you find that you''re in trouble.\n\nBut if you''re open, surrender to the lord. If ticket comes, we go. If it doesn''t come, we will not go now.\n\nWe sit down. I''m trying to use the word importance. It is of more importance to him than you.\n\nHe''s the one that is asking you to go. So why should you now go and do or die to buy a ticket? No. It''s you that is doing or dying, not him.\n\nIf he wants you to be in UK, you''ll be there. I used to advise some of our people here in UK. Many people who follow crooked ways to stay.\n\nI said, no. The fact that you desire to be here, means that the lord wants you to be here. Because you have the lord inside.\n\nThe king is inside you. And if that desire is desiring to be here, please my brother, go home. Go home, do the right thing, you''ll be back here.\n\nProperly. Without fear of anybody. And it''s not once.\n\nMany people have taken that advice. And they''ve seen the lord in action. Because sometimes we want to do it by ourselves.\n\nBut we forget that the king is in here. And he does all things right. Okay.\n\nAlright. So. I want to.\n\nI was saying that Jesus did not preach anything else apart from the kingdom. John the Baptist came, preached the kingdom. When Jesus came, he also preached about the kingdom of God.\n\nIt''s here. It''s no longer near. It''s here.\n\nBecause it''s been fulfilled in him. He is the king. That is eternally, immortal, the only true God.\n\nThe lord Jesus Christ. That''s all he preached. What did his disciples preach? What did the apostles like Paul, what did they preach? The only thing, please.\n\nNo matter what you.'
 where service_date = '2026-08-23' and title = 'Living Under The Rule Of The KING';

-- ============================================================
-- PART 3 of 4 - the 12-point outline
-- ============================================================
delete from sermon_points where sermon_id = (select id from sermons where service_date = '2026-08-23' and title = 'Living Under The Rule Of The KING');
insert into sermon_points (sermon_id, position, heading, detail, scriptures)
values
    ((select id from sermons where service_date = '2026-08-23' and title = 'Living Under The Rule Of The KING'), 1, E'Kingdom means king plus domain', E'Not somewhere far away. A domain, a realm, an area where the king is ruling. He keeps returning to this definition because everything else in the message depends on the kingdom being a present realm rather than a future destination.', '{Luke 17:20-21}'),
    ((select id from sermons where service_date = '2026-08-23' and title = 'Living Under The Rule Of The KING'), 2, E'Why Jesus taught in parables', E'A parable is a provocation, not a decoration. To those who have ears and do not hear it closes the matter. But if it wakes a desire to know more, He runs to meet you immediately - and that, he says, is exactly why the Lord taught this way.', '{Matthew 13:10-13}'),
    ((select id from sermons where service_date = '2026-08-23' and title = 'Living Under The Rule Of The KING'), 3, E'The treasure and the pearl: both men responded with joy', E'Recap of 9 August. The man who found treasure in a field reburied it, sold his house and his business and bought the whole field so he would contest with nobody. The merchant who found one pearl of great price did the same. The detail he wants noticed is not the selling, it is the joy.', '{Matthew 13:44,Matthew 13:45-46}'),
    ((select id from sermons where service_date = '2026-08-23' and title = 'Living Under The Rule Of The KING'), 4, E'Your soul is worth more than the world', E'What will it profit a man to gain the whole world and lose his soul. His reading: the Lord is saying one soul is worth more to Him than the whole world. Hold that next to whatever circumstance you are facing and the circumstance shrinks - the travail will finish, and you will walk through it unharmed.', '{Matthew 16:26}'),
    ((select id from sermons where service_date = '2026-08-23' and title = 'Living Under The Rule Of The KING'), 5, E'The pearl is the King already inside you', E'He asks the question and answers it plainly. That pearl is inside you right now - the precious Holy Spirit, the King eternal, the King immortal, the only true God. You have found it whether you believe it or not. Not a distant reward and not an abstraction.', '{Colossians 1:27,Luke 17:21}'),
    ((select id from sermons where service_date = '2026-08-23' and title = 'Living Under The Rule Of The KING'), 6, E'The Christian dilemma: our response does not match', E'THE TURN OF THE SERMON. We appear to have found the kingdom, but our response does not support it. At best it is timid, at best lukewarm, at best civilised - dismissed as not a big deal, or warned against as getting carried away. Not from doubt: because we do not know the value of what is inside us.', '{Matthew 13:44,Matthew 13:45-46}'),
    ((select id from sermons where service_date = '2026-08-23' and title = 'Living Under The Rule Of The KING'), 7, E'Seek first, and the kingdom is the pathway to abundant life', E'He will not prioritise your life for you; only you can take that decision. Seek first the kingdom and the rest is added. And the kingdom is not the thing that costs you the good life - it is the road to it. Christ is a true king, and a true king takes care of his citizens: what they wear, what they eat, where they live. If He feeds the birds, what about the only creature made in His image?', '{Matthew 6:33,John 10:10,Matthew 6:26}'),
    ((select id from sermons where service_date = '2026-08-23' and title = 'Living Under The Rule Of The KING'), 8, E'Entered by a new birth', E'The morning''s reading. Born of water is the physical birth into this realm; born again is the second birth into the spirit realm. Nicodemus got lost because he assumed a second birth into the same realm. So also into the kingdom of God you have to be born.', '{John 3:3,John 3:5,John 3:7}'),
    ((select id from sermons where service_date = '2026-08-23' and title = 'Living Under The Rule Of The KING'), 9, E'The evidence of new birth is obedience', E'If you believe what Christ did on the cross you no longer live for yourself. The King inside wants to rule, and ruling works through hearing and obeying his word - put as a line hard to argue with: if you hear his word and you don''t obey it, he''s not ruling, you are ruling. The song at the altar call, I surrender all, is the de facto effect of new birth.', '{Galatians 2:20,James 4:7}'),
    ((select id from sermons where service_date = '2026-08-23' and title = 'Living Under The Rule Of The KING'), 10, E'The Spirit is already inside and waiting on your response', E'He will teach you all things and bring everything to your remembrance. Every decision facing you, He already knows; He is waiting only on your response. His testimony is that guidance arrived unprompted - he cannot point back to fasting and prayer before the Spirit spoke, because something was threatening God''s destiny for him and the information simply came.', '{John 14:26,Romans 8:14}'),
    ((select id from sermons where service_date = '2026-08-23' and title = 'Living Under The Rule Of The KING'), 11, E'Repentance is a change of direction, not a mood', E'John the Baptist preached the kingdom is near, change your mind - and changing your mind means changing your perspective on life. You are walking one way; you must stop and go toward where the kingdom is. And it is not a distant dream to be entered at death. It is here now. That is why the change is urgent.', '{Matthew 3:2,Mark 1:15}'),
    ((select id from sermons where service_date = '2026-08-23' and title = 'Living Under The Rule Of The KING'), 12, E'He does not send you to war at your own cost', E'His own story. Chasing an executive directorship at a bank, his heart moving toward money because money was ruling, and being shown both that this was not the plan and what waited at the end of that road. He stopped, was called into missions about two weeks later, and has drawn no salary from anyone since 1998. If the King sends you, He has already paid the cost; the trouble starts when you decide to do or die to arrange it yourself. SEE NOTES - the war-at-your-own-cost line is Paul, not Jesus.', '{1 Corinthians 9:7}');

